<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paulo Dias de Novais</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510–1589</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paulo Dias de Novais was a Portuguese nobleman and grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartolomeu-dias">Bartolomeu Dias</a> who founded the colony of Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>. Arriving in 1575 with a royal charter to conquer the Kingdom of Ndongo, he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> in 1576 and began the long wars with Ndongo that fed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paulo-dias-de-novais.jpg" alt="Paulo Dias de Novais" width="249" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post of Angola · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stamp_of_Angola_-_1948_-_Colnect_329380_-_Paulo_Dias_de_Novais_1510-1589_colonizer.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
